---
title: Mortadella, burrata and pistachio sandwich
servings: 1
yield: 1 sandwich
tags: [italian, pork, quick]
cuisine: italian
source: Mortadella and Burrata Sandwich with Pistachio Pesto by Elizabeth Nyland, Edible Vancouver Island, https://ediblevancouverisland.ediblecommunities.com/recipes/mortadella-and-burrata-sandwich-pistachio-pesto
---

== Pistachio pesto ==

Blend the @pistachios{3/4%cup}(roasted, salted), @basil{1/2%cup}(loosely packed leaves),
@parmesan cheese{1/2%cup}(grated),
@extra virgin olive oil{1/2%cup}, @garlic{1%clove}(small) and the juice of the
@lemon{1/2} in a #food processor{} until smooth. Season with @kosher salt{} and
@black pepper{}.

== Sandwich ==

Split the @focaccia{1%piece}(6- to 8-inch square) like a bun. Pizza bianca
works too.

Cut the @burrata{1}(large) into small pieces in a #small bowl{} with a knife
and fork, so the creamy middle mixes with the outer skin. Season with
@flaky sea salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Spread the burrata over the bottom half. Lay on a handful of @arugula{} and the
@mortadella{4%slices}.

Spread 2 to 4 tablespoons of the pesto on the top half. Close it, cut it in
half on the diagonal and eat.

> The pesto makes more than one sandwich needs; it keeps a few days in the
> fridge under a film of oil.
